    zh-TW patch 034: pickup notification text over planet exploration area
    
    Moves the mineral / life / energy pickup pop-up text out of the RADAR
    mini-map corner and into the planet-exploration area, centred ~30 px
    above the lander sprite (which is always at the map centre).
    
    Before (v1.0.4):
      ScrollPlanetSide()'s NumFrames branch (which draws the 3-line pickup
      notification) still ran in the outer RadarContext set at ScrollPlanetSide
      top, and computed baselines with (RADAR_WIDTH >> 1, RES_SCALE(8)).
      Players' eyes stayed on the lander during pickup, so the text popping
      up in the bottom-right radar corner was easy to miss.
    
    After (this patch):
      1. Save the outer context and switch to PlanetContext for just the text
         draw block; restore both at the end so the subsequent
         RedrawSurfaceScan / DrawRadarBorder / RotatePlanetSphere calls are
         unaffected.
      2. Save + set PlyrFont locally, restore afterward (matches the pattern
         used elsewhere in the file for context-scoped state).
      3. Place baseline.x at MapSurface.width >> 1 (horizontal centre of the
         planet-exploration view).
      4. Place baseline.y at (MapSurface.height >> 1) - RES_SCALE(30) so the
         three-line stack sits just above the lander sprite without covering
         it.
      5. Lines 2 and 3 continue to stack down by RES_SCALE(7) each — same
         spacing as the previous position.
    
    Impact scope:
      - Behaviour is identical for PC and 3DO font modes; the outer branch
        used to differ only in which context ScrollPlanetSide had already
        activated, and this patch overrides that locally for the text block.
      - Nothing else uses these MineralText baselines at draw time; they are
        reset at the start of every pickup event.
      - Non-zh-TW players receive the same behavioural change (the text is
        a gameplay HUD element, not localised strings). If we later want to
        keep this addon-only, the block can be wrapped in an addon check;
        for now it is unconditional to keep the change minimal.
    
    Patch file: uqm-work/patches/034-lander-pickup-text-over-planet.patch

